@meta
id: 17-03
title: What counts as a jump
chapter: 17
type: lesson
skills: jumplist
par: 56
minutes: 6
vscode: no equivalent; the back button only knows about navigation
open: order.provider.ts

@brief
Both `ship` and `cancel` need an `actorId: string` parameter added to
their signatures, for the audit log.

Search for `ship(` to land on the first signature. Do not edit it yet.
Get to `cancel` by pressing the paragraph-forward key four separate
times, then one `j`. Add the parameter there.

Now look at the jumplist with `:jumps` before you go back. There are
four new entries, one per paragraph key, because `}` is a jump and each
press was a separate one. `j` is not a jump and added nothing.

Come back to `ship` in one command and add the parameter there too.
The edit is identical, so the dot command will do the typing.

@keys
| `}` | forward a paragraph; a jump, every single press |
| `4}` | four paragraphs; one jump |
| `j` `w` `f` | not jumps, never recorded |
| `:jumps` | show the jumplist; `>` marks where you are in it |
| `4` `Ctrl-O` | back four entries in one go |
| `.` | repeat the last change |

@hints
`:jumps` lists the entries with the newest at the bottom. Count the
lines between the `>` and the `ship(` line and that is your number.
--
`Ctrl-O` takes a count, exactly like a motion. `4` then `Ctrl-O` is four
steps back in one command.
--
`/ship(` Enter, `}` `}` `}` `}` `j`, `f)i, actorId: string` Esc,
`:jumps` Enter, `4` `Ctrl-O`, `f)` and `.`.

@solution
    /ship(<Enter> }}}}j f)i, actorId: string<Esc>
    :jumps<Enter> 4 Ctrl-O f). :wq<Enter>

The rule for what gets recorded is simple once you have seen it: a
motion is a jump if it could carry you an unpredictable distance. Search
(`/` `?` `n` `N` `*` `#`), `G` and `gg`, `%`, `{` and `}`, `(` and
`)`, `H` `M` `L`, marks, and every buffer switch. Everything that moves
a known small amount, `hjkl`, `w` `b` `e`, `f` `t`, `0` `^` `$`, is not
a jump and leaves nothing behind.

The consequence you just saw: `}}}}` is four jumps, `4}` is one. Both
land in the same place, but the way back is four presses versus one.
When you know how far you are going, put the count on the motion and
the jumplist stays tidy.

`:jumps` is worth reading once so you trust it. The newest entry is at
the bottom, `>` shows where you currently sit, and the number on each
line is exactly the count to give `Ctrl-O`. The list is saved between
sessions, so yours will be longer than four lines and may stop at a
`-- More --` prompt; `q` closes it. Once you have seen it a few times
you will stop looking and just press `Ctrl-O` until the screen looks
right, which is how everybody actually uses it.

`f).` at the end is the small habit worth keeping: come back to the
exact spot, then let `.` do the typing you already did once.

@start order.provider.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';
import { OrderRepository } from './order.repository';
import { CustomerProvider } from '../customer/customer.provider';
import { PaymentService } from '../../infrastructure/services/payment.service';
import { EmailService } from '../../infrastructure/services/email.service';

@injectable()
export class OrderProvider {
  constructor(
    @inject(OrderRepository) protected orderRepository: OrderRepository,
    @inject(CustomerProvider) protected customerProvider: CustomerProvider,
    @inject(PaymentService) protected paymentService: PaymentService,
    @inject(EmailService) protected emailService: EmailService,
  ) {}

  public async findOne(id: string) {
    const order = await this.orderRepository.findOne({ where: { id } });

    if (!order) {
      throw exception('ORDER_NOT_FOUND');
    }

    return order;
  }

  public async findByCustomer(customerId: string) {
    await this.customerProvider.findOne(customerId);

    return this.orderRepository.findByCustomer({ customerId });
  }

  public async create(args: { customerId: string; total: number }) {
    const customer = await this.customerProvider.findOne(args.customerId);

    const order = await this.orderRepository.create({
      values: { customerId: customer.id, total: args.total, status: 'PENDING' },
    });

    await this.emailService.send({ orderId: order.id, template: 'order_confirmation' });

    return order;
  }

  public async ship(id: string) {
    const order = await this.findOne(id);

    if (order.status !== 'PENDING') {
      throw exception('ORDER_NOT_PENDING');
    }

    await this.orderRepository.update({ where: { id }, values: { status: 'SHIPPED' } });

    return order;
  }

  public async cancel(id: string) {
    const order = await this.findOne(id);

    if (order.status === 'SHIPPED') {
      throw exception('ORDER_ALREADY_SHIPPED');
    }

    await this.paymentService.refund(order.id);

    return this.orderRepository.update({
      where: { id },
      values: { status: 'CANCELLED' },
    });
  }
}

@expected order.provider.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';
import { OrderRepository } from './order.repository';
import { CustomerProvider } from '../customer/customer.provider';
import { PaymentService } from '../../infrastructure/services/payment.service';
import { EmailService } from '../../infrastructure/services/email.service';

@injectable()
export class OrderProvider {
  constructor(
    @inject(OrderRepository) protected orderRepository: OrderRepository,
    @inject(CustomerProvider) protected customerProvider: CustomerProvider,
    @inject(PaymentService) protected paymentService: PaymentService,
    @inject(EmailService) protected emailService: EmailService,
  ) {}

  public async findOne(id: string) {
    const order = await this.orderRepository.findOne({ where: { id } });

    if (!order) {
      throw exception('ORDER_NOT_FOUND');
    }

    return order;
  }

  public async findByCustomer(customerId: string) {
    await this.customerProvider.findOne(customerId);

    return this.orderRepository.findByCustomer({ customerId });
  }

  public async create(args: { customerId: string; total: number }) {
    const customer = await this.customerProvider.findOne(args.customerId);

    const order = await this.orderRepository.create({
      values: { customerId: customer.id, total: args.total, status: 'PENDING' },
    });

    await this.emailService.send({ orderId: order.id, template: 'order_confirmation' });

    return order;
  }

  public async ship(id: string, actorId: string) {
    const order = await this.findOne(id);

    if (order.status !== 'PENDING') {
      throw exception('ORDER_NOT_PENDING');
    }

    await this.orderRepository.update({ where: { id }, values: { status: 'SHIPPED' } });

    return order;
  }

  public async cancel(id: string, actorId: string) {
    const order = await this.findOne(id);

    if (order.status === 'SHIPPED') {
      throw exception('ORDER_ALREADY_SHIPPED');
    }

    await this.paymentService.refund(order.id);

    return this.orderRepository.update({
      where: { id },
      values: { status: 'CANCELLED' },
    });
  }
}
